    feeds: ["recovery from work", "unhurried family time", "shared ritual"],
    description:
      "Survey research among Sabbath-keepers finds observance associated with better mental and physical health, mediated by lower stress and religious coping; interview studies of observant Jews and of women who adopted a Sabbath describe rest, contemplation and deepened relationships, and a study of 1,300 teachers found Sabbath-keeping inversely related to burnout. Occupational health research shows that weekend recovery — detaching from work, low-effort and social activities — predicts mood, health and job performance in the following week. The boundary: the Sabbath studies are cross-sectional or qualitative and mostly religious samples; the recovery literature is stronger but about work, not families.",
